MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_001: Vermin are typically speedy, and you are no\nexception! Tch. Die, won't you?
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_002: Fabio, look out! Haaah!
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_003: That should be the last of them. I'll have the others\nsearch for foes lying in ambush.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_004: I did not require your help, but I suppose you do\ndeserve my thanks.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_005: Considering you once despised me, I find\nmyself moved.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_006: With regard to this battle, I aided you because I was\nin a position to.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_007: Master Long taught me that when there is someone\nin need, the right thing to do is to help them.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_008: So you simply did as you were taught, and\nnothing more.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_009: That's right. If it wasn't for his teachings, I wouldn't\nhave stepped in.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_010: I see. So your opinion of me has not changed.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_011: Even though our interests now align, and we have\nbecome allies.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_012: You have not yet fully severed your ties with Vritra.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_013: Furthermore, even if our interests align, I'm not\nrequired to like you.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_014: True enough, though perhaps rude to say aloud. You\nhave not changed. It is strange, though.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_015: What is?
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_016: If you dislike me so, why not simply avoid me?
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_017: The battlefield is wide, after all. Why fight nearby\none you detest?
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_018: Well. To keep watch over you.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_019: There's no telling what you might share with Vritra,\nafter all. I'll be going now.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_C_020: To keep watch over me, she says, as she leaves. And\nI had thought the Mediators flawless beings.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_001: I had thought you were gazing at the moon and\nseething with hatred for Vritra all the while.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_002: Yet it seems that is not the case. Your eyes\nare gentle.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_003: Vritra remains my enemy, of course, but these days\nI'm usually reflecting on Master Long's teachings.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_004: The sun and the moon appear as circles—the\nultimate form. One must feel them flowing within.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_005: Circles are boundless. To attain the secret technique\nhe taught me, I must remember this.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_006: The first time I witnessed your use of that technique,\nI was taken aback.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_007: I found myself staring in wonder at your fusion of\nlost technology and martial arts.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_008: To look at the moon and think not of Vritra, but of\nyour learnings...
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_009: It seems Master Long means much to you.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_010: Are you implying that it is strange for a Mediator to\nfeel deeply for a loved one who died?
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_011: No. I empathize. I myself have someone I feel\nstrongly for.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_012: I see... You know, Master Long was like a father\nto me.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_013: Even though I should despise you, I protected you.\nDo you recall that?
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_014: Indeed. It left an impression—all the more because \nyour explanation was unsatisfactory.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_015: At the time, I didn't even understand my feelings.\nBut now I do.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_016: Intriguing. Please, divulge, if you would.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_017: Certainly—in fact, I want you to hear it. I cannot\nmove forward unless I share with you.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_018: Fabio, every now and then, I see flashes of Master\nLong in you.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_019: You speak in an unpleasant and sarcastic manner,\nbut your words provoke thought.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_020: You provide me with a shift in perspective akin to\nMaster Long's lessons.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_021: His teachings are with me always...as are the feelings\nI have for my friends.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_022: And so, it's critical that someone like you—an\noutsider—continues to challenge me.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_023: So now that you have internalized his teachings and\nlead your people, you use me to test your thinking.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_024: Yes. Finding the answers to my problems in the face\nof your unkind questions leads to my growth.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_025: So, you are not a friend to me, but I do find your\npresence in my life has value.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_026: Well. Though I find myself disquieted by the\nassertion I am no friend of yours, I can accept it.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_027: As I now understand that you have accepted me...\nI am pleased to continue to enumerate your failings.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_028: If my questions spur your growth this way, then\nperhaps you could say I am a father figure to you.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_029: Your reasoning is beyond flawed! I certainly do not\nsee you that way.
MID_SE_Anh_Fab_B_030: Ahahaha. Do you not? Yet try as you might, you\ncannot refute it!